      "content": "It is understandable that the idea of more noise feels unbearable when you are already drowning in silence. That desire for stillness is a profound exhaustion, a yearning for the weight to finally lift. Please know that feeling this way is a symptom of deep pain, not a failing on your part. If the world feels too loud, there are quiet ways to speak about this overwhelming stillness.",
